## 15. Open Product and Engineering Decisions

The following decisions remain unresolved and should be documented as they are investigated.

| Decision | Why it matters |
|---|---|
| Desktop capture mechanism | Determines how the live game view reaches the analysis engine |
| Continuous-analysis refresh policy | Balances responsiveness, computational cost, and prediction stability |
| Desktop interface technology | Determines the UI implementation and integration approach |
| Study-library storage | Determines how images, checkpoints, and results persist |
| Geographic knowledge sources | Determines the provenance and reliability of clue associations |
| Regional hierarchy | Determines how regional guesses are represented and evaluated |
| Scoring calibration | Determines whether scores can eventually be interpreted as probabilities |
| Minimum evidence thresholds | Determines when GeoMeta should report insufficient evidence |
| Privacy and retention behavior | Determines how captured images and study records are managed |
| Live-use compatibility | Determines which gameplay environments and use cases can be supported |

These decisions should be resolved through focused investigation and recorded in the relevant technical documentation. They do not prevent us from defining the product's purpose and intended behavior now.

